    keys: ["Grade × thickness view", "Intercept cut-off / Minimum length (m) / Max internal dilution (m) / Within a logged unit", "GT cut-off / Density (t/m³) / Panel side (m)"],
    summary: "Reduces each hole's intercepts to a thickness and a grade × thickness (GT), drawn and contoured in plan or on a long section. Opened from Grade estimation.",
    more: "For a thin, flat body or a steep vein or lode drilled by many holes. Opened with Grade × thickness, in plan or on a long section…, in the Grade estimation pane. Intercepts follow the same rules as Best intercepts, from a cut-off you type; nothing is assumed about the deposit. There is no declustering, no classification and no resource category. Type the intercept cut-off, and the GT cut-off for the contour and the totals. A hole assayed with no intercept is drilled ground that tested barren at your cut-off.",
